${macro.generated_by(self.path)}

=[ Tomet Wiki ]

Wiki system for the Tomet ecosystem.

==[ Overview ]

`tomet-wiki` is a Wiki engine and static site generator designed for Tomet documents, featuring inline editing support with conflict resolution and Git CMS integration.

==[ Usage ]

```bash
tomet-wiki init [dir] [--title <title>] [--owner <owner>] [--repo <repo>]
tomet-wiki build [dir] [-d/--dest <dest>] [--strict] [--production]
tomet-wiki serve [dir] [-d/--dest <dest>] [--host <ip>] [-p/--port <port>] [--production]
```

==[ Configuration (`wiki.toml`) ]

A `wiki.toml` configuration file in the vault root controls site generation and CMS authentication:

```toml
[wiki]
title = "My Wiki"
lang = "ja"
dest = "dist"

[cms]
owner = "my-org"
repo = "my-wiki"
branch = "main"
path_prefix = "docs"
auth_endpoint = "https://auth.tomet.dev/github"

[build]
url_prefix = "/wiki"
exclude = [
  "00-09 System/01 Apps"
]
```

==[ Workspace Layout ]

-| @dir(crates/tomet-wiki-headless) (`tomet-wiki-headless`) -- Headless Wiki engine composing `tomet-shelf-*` component crates. Owns `WikiConfig`, `build_wiki`, and `WikiDevHandler`.
-| @dir(crates/tomet-wiki-assets) (`tomet-wiki-assets`) -- Wiki viewing theme and asset bundle.
-| @dir(app) (`tomet-wiki`) -- Main CLI binary (`build`, `serve`, `init`).

==[ Theme & Reading Experience ]

`tomet-wiki-assets` provides an Askama-based theme tailored specifically for wikis and digital gardens:

-| Single-Column Focused Reading: Eliminates book-style sidebar hierarchies and linear previous/next pagination in favor of organic graph navigation.
-| First-Class Backlinks: Automatic presentation of incoming references at the footer of each document.
-| Inline Conflict Visualization: Dedicated presentation for `.tm-conflict` blocks, clearly distinguishing local and remote versions with badge indicators.
-| Editor & CMS Integration: Injects `data-tmt-rel-path`, `window.tmtWikiCms`, and the `#tmt-wiki-editor-root` container for Svelte editor components.

==[ Building and Testing ]

=== Build workspace

```bash
just build
```

=== Build Svelte 5 editor bundle

```bash
just wasm          # build the editor's own WebAssembly (crates/tomet-wiki-wasm)
just editor        # `just wasm`, then compile the Svelte 5 editor island via Deno into assets/
just editor-check  # verify assets are up to date with sources
```

The editor's WebAssembly is built here, not taken from a package: `tomet-wiki-wasm` carries the GitHub client and conflict functions of `tomet-cms-js` and its own `highlightSpans` (syntax colors from `tomet::highlight`, offsets in UTF-16 code units), and is inlined into `wiki-editor.js`. The dev shell provides the `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target and `wasm-bindgen`.

=== Run tests

```bash
just test
```

=== Check code

```bash
just check
just clippy
```

=== Documentation

```bash
just docs        # regenerate Markdown from tmtroot/
just docs-check  # verify docs match exports
```
